From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:32:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Type multiline text annotations in the viewport

Text annotations can now be typed directly in the viewport with the
new Type Text In Viewport operator (Alt+T in the annotation tool, or
the button in the Text panel). Enter starts a new line, Tab inserts a
tab and Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I toggle markdown bold and italic on the word
at the caret. Ctrl+Enter or a left click saves, Esc cancels.

Printed text now keeps what was typed: each line of a literal is
parsed on its own, so blank lines, indentation, tabs, repeated spaces
and lines starting with "1." or "#" are no longer dropped or merged,
and a literal after a multiline one no longer overlaps it. The
viewport preview handles tabs and the \n escape the same way.

Fixes #6427

